{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":346764,"duration_api_ms":343416,"num_turns":24,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e93f2599-56cf-4dee-840a-df2195427453","total_cost_usd":1.70113625,"usage":{"input_tokens":8215,"cache_creation_input_tokens":123279,"cache_read_input_tokens":1009985,"output_tokens":15383,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":123279,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":8215,"outputTokens":15383,"cacheReadInputTokens":1009985,"cacheCreationInputTokens":123279,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.70113625,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"CleanFilter action in engine.rs:346-368 silently destroys nitrogen and carbon: microbe biomass is reduced by `intensity * 0.5` but the removed mass is not routed to any pool (fine_detritus, DON/DOC, etc.). This is an N/C conservation violation. The removed biomass should be routed to `fine_detritus_g_total` via `live_biomass_detrital_mass_g()` (same pattern used for shrimp mortality at shrimp.rs:483-491), or alternatively tracked as an explicit budget export if the intent is that filter-rinsing removes matter from the system entirely.","rationale":"The budget ledger will correctly record the mass loss as a negative net delta on the CleanFilter tick, but the loss is unexplained — it appears as conservation breakage rather than a classified export. Downstream bead tanksim-6e5.3.4 (audit feeding/detritus/DOC/mineralization bookkeeping) will flag this as an unaccounted sink if not fixed before that audit runs."},{"body":"Conservation tests (test_closed_system_c_conservation, test_closed_system_n_conservation) only exercise the code-default ProcessParams which sets `respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour = 0.0` and `photosynthesis_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour = 0.0` (process.rs:187-188). The actual data preset (default.toml:9-10) sets these to 0.08 and 0.12 respectively. When loaded from presets, the chemistry system (chemistry.rs:31-47) adds/removes DIC without a compensating organic-C change, breaking carbon conservation by milligrams per tick. Add a comment or separate test acknowledging that the hourly DIC respiration/photosynthesis flux is an intentional atmospheric-exchange simplification and that closed-system carbon conservation holds only when these rates are zero.","rationale":"The current tests give false confidence that carbon is conserved in gameplay scenarios. Dependent bead tanksim-6e5.1.2.2 (debug hooks and test helpers for budget inspection) will build on these conservation tests. If a future contributor loads a process preset into a conservation test and it fails, there's no documentation explaining the expected behavior, leading to wasted debugging time."},{"body":"SiphonDetritus action in engine.rs:342-346 silently destroys nitrogen and carbon: `particulate_organics_g_total` and `fine_detritus_g_total` are reduced by `fraction` without routing the removed mass anywhere. Like CleanFilter, this is a physical export that should either be routed explicitly or return a BudgetDelta with the export amount so the ledger records a classified outflow rather than an unexplained mass loss.","rationale":"Same pattern as CleanFilter — the budget snapshot comparison will show the delta, but without explicit in/out classification the ledger cannot distinguish intentional export from a conservation bug. The tanksim-6e5.3.4 end-to-end bookkeeping audit will need this distinction."}],"summary":"The budget tracking implementation is solid overall. The BudgetLedger, BudgetSnapshot, and per-system delta recording in engine.rs are well-structured. The canonical `total_nitrogen_mg()` and `total_carbon_mg()` helpers in budget.rs correctly cover all N- and C-bearing pools including substrate nutrient stores, and the `test_budget_component_labels_cover_all_element_bearing_fields` test provides a structural guard against missing pools. The zero-cost runtime gating via `Option<BudgetLedger>` satisfies the acceptance criterion. All 12 budget_tracking tests and 10 concentration_helpers tests pass.\n\nThree correctness issues found: (1) CleanFilter action destroys microbe N/C without routing it, (2) carbon conservation tests rely on zero DIC rates that differ from actual presets, and (3) SiphonDetritus similarly destroys detritus N/C without routing. Issues 1 and 3 are physical exports that should be explicitly classified in the budget rather than appearing as unexplained mass loss."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a4c54f85-64bb-4cf1-a666-080bfb47505f"}
